  "description": "WOQFAJ crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R 3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C30 H70 Gd4 N6 O23 6+,6(Cl1 O4 1-),6(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.854-3.863 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.26-108.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4(Hpro)4(pro)2(μ3-OH)4(H2O)7](ClO4)6·6H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 7 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
